    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d452-a2">

                <pb facs="0836" n="822" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg822"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center"><seg type="margin">[123]</seg> *[Inclosure No.
                        2.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Goodrich, surveyor,
                        to Mr. Moore, collector.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Custom-House,
                            Philadelphia</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Surveyor’s
                        Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1869-11-09"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">November</hi> 9, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In compliance with the request contained in
                    your letter of this date, I have caused an examination of the ram Atlanta to be
                    made, now lying at Neafie &amp; Levy’s wharf, in charge of officers of the
                    customs.</p>
                <p>The Atlanta has recently been repaired, and her machinery put in order. During
                    the last week four large guns have been taken on, which are placed in position,
                    and mounted.</p>
                <p>She has no coal, stores, nor ammunition on board, but could be got ready for sea
                    in four or five days. Two inspectors are in charge of the ram.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. O. GOODRICH,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Surveyor</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry D. Moore</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Collector.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
